---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro'
import BlogPostShell from '../../components/BlogPostShell.astro'
import BlogToolEmbed from '../../components/BlogToolEmbed.astro'

const slug = 'amount-of-substance-converter'
const seo = {
  title: 'Mole converter — mol, mmol, µmol | maratool',
  description: 'Convert moles, millimoles, micromoles, and pound-moles instantly. Free browser amount-of-substance converter.',
  canonical: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
  schema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BlogPosting',
    headline: 'How to convert moles, millimoles, and micromoles',
    image: 'https://maratool.com/og/converter.svg',
    datePublished: '2026-07-25',
    dateModified: '2026-07-25',
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Marcell Almeida', url: 'https://marcell.com.br' },
    publisher: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'maratool',
      url: 'https://maratool.com',
      logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://maratool.com/favicon.svg' },
    },
    mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    url: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
    description: 'Convert moles, millimoles, micromoles, and pound-moles instantly. Free browser amount-of-substance converter.',
  },
  breadcrumbSchema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://maratool.com' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://maratool.com/blog' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'How to convert moles, millimoles, and micromoles', item: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    ],
  },
}
---
<Base {...seo}>
  <Layout>
    <BlogPostShell
      title="How to convert moles, millimoles, and micromoles"
      lead="Type an amount — read mol, mmol, µmol, nmol, or lb-mol instantly."
      date="July 25, 2026"
      dateIso="2026-07-25"
    >
      <p>Lab protocols quote mmol, clinical chemistry reports µmol/L, and reagent bottles list mol. The <a href="/amount-of-substance-converter/">Amount of Substance Converter</a> shifts between mole prefixes without mental exponent math.</p>

      <BlogToolEmbed slug="amount-of-substance-converter" title="Try it — convert amount of substance units" height={440} />

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Pick units</strong> — "Millimole (mmol)" to "Mole (mol)", or any other pair.</li>
        <li><strong>Type a value</strong> — the result updates as you type, with swap and copy.</li>
        <li><strong>Copy</strong> — one click, with "Copied!" feedback.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Amount of substance conversion factors</h2>
      <p>Every unit converts through the mole (the base unit). To convert A → B, multiply by A's factor and divide by B's:</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Unit</th><th>= this many moles</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        <tr><td>Kilomole (kmol)</td><td>1,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Mole (mol)</td><td>1</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Millimole (mmol)</td><td>0.001</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Micromole (µmol)</td><td>1.0000 × 10^-6</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Nanomole (nmol)</td><td>1.0000 × 10^-9</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Picomole (pmol)</td><td>1.0000 × 10^-12</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pound-mole (lb-mol)</td><td>453.59237</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>When you need it</h2>
      <p>Typical scales: a PCR primer stock might be 100 µmol/L, a glucose panel reads ~5 mmol/L, and a synthesis batch uses 0.5 mol. To go from amount to mass, multiply moles by molar mass — see the <a href="/molar-mass-converter/">Molar Mass Converter</a>.</p>

      <h2>Sources & methodology</h2>
      <p>Conversion factors follow <a href="https://www.bipm.org/en/publications/si-brochure" rel="noopener" target="_blank">BIPM SI Brochure</a>; exact-by-definition factors are marked in the tool itself. All math runs client-side in your browser — nothing is uploaded.</p>

      <h2>More conversion guides</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/blog/molar-mass-converter/">How to convert molar mass units (g/mol, kg/mol, Da)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/density-converter/">How to convert density between kg/m³, g/cm³, and lb/ft³</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/dynamic-viscosity-converter/">How to convert centipoise to Pa·s (dynamic viscosity)</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Or browse everything at once in the <a href="/blog/new-unit-converters/">new unit &amp; sizing converters roundup</a>.</p>

      <hr class="blog-divider" />
      <p class="blog-footer-note">The <a href="/amount-of-substance-converter/">Amount of Substance</a> tool is free, runs locally, and never sends your data to a server. More <a href="/converter/">converter tools</a> at <a href="/">maratool.com</a>.</p>
    </BlogPostShell>
  </Layout>
</Base>
